  "structure": {
    "block_count": 50,
    "blocks": [
      {
        "block_id": "block_000000",
        "block_index": 0,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h1",
        "text": "Best High-Fiber Foods for Toddlers and Kids",
        "text_sha256": "286f65aa2ffb458cbd407ff91a922113672dafd4fcab03b244fe8e4517e50f32",
        "word_count": 7
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000001",
        "block_index": 1,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "best high-fiber foods for kids",
        "text_sha256": "b7fac57da9e72156c872db8b471b993b0e839915bc375d0a14244aec383001d5",
        "word_count": 5
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000002",
        "block_index": 2,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Fiber is incredibly important for your growing tot. Check out the best fiber-rich foods for toddlers and kids here, plus delicious ways to serve it up.",
        "text_sha256": "ab45376da00c20858aad54c7c7c0cf1932fe806900c8eca96c22792899c85125",
        "word_count": 26
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000003",
        "block_index": 3,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "When you’re planning your toddler's meals , you probably pay close attention to the big three: fat, calories and sugar. But you should also consider dietary fiber — and not just because it will help keep your little one regular.",
        "text_sha256": "ab9b6591bdd3c7a5ff7053fcf48723647eed150fde57ecb66ac654fc5b680b4d",
        "word_count": 40
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000004",
        "block_index": 4,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "In children (and adults — so take note, parents!), fiber can help increase feelings of fullness, which can help kids maintain a healthy weight. A high-fiber diet can also help prevent heart disease and diabetes.",
        "text_sha256": "a006301cfbb0f1339b02aadb2b533619ea05131de589066f21b4057ee3c0fb7d",
        "word_count": 35
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000005",
        "block_index": 5,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Still, despite the benefits of fiber, reports show that most kids in the United States aren’t getting enough. Here’s more on the benefits of fiber, plus the best high-fiber foods for tots.",
        "text_sha256": "44c52c4accc4efc60baf056c8ef9ba73585c7f16fcdcc05fb727a86352f5f08f",
        "word_count": 32
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000006",
        "block_index": 6,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "What is fiber?",
        "text_sha256": "7266cf8f94b53c5207410724b3d723c36601fd9b0f7653fe9299435ad30be842",
        "word_count": 3
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000007",
        "block_index": 7,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Fiber is a type of carbohydrate that’s found in fruits, vegetables and whole grains. There are two types of fiber:",
        "text_sha256": "1c85e090d57018582f4c3e24acc7e8f80b5457ffe4718efb940bb86bc445b60e",
        "word_count": 20
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000008",
        "block_index": 8,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Soluble fiber, which dissolves in water to form a gel-like substance, slowing digestion and helping to lower cholesterol levels and blood sugar levels.",
        "text_sha256": "cf17b7906c04c88d49786d2136c625280d8b26e73f3b45807745e088ec024366",
        "word_count": 23
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000009",
        "block_index": 9,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Insoluble fiber, which bulks up your stool and helps regulate bowel movements.",
        "text_sha256": "eee719de77178db7170c05f316dcf6812cf16fff59efabb127265091e87bf418",
        "word_count": 12
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000010",
        "block_index": 10,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "Why do toddlers need fiber?",
        "text_sha256": "7725f074106ea26828d16682d0c73dc9c440de3288a8a9752bb26f425f1dfc99",
        "word_count": 5
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000011",
        "block_index": 11,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Research shows that when kids eat more fiber, they eat less fat and sugar. That’s because fiber-rich foods — those with at least 3 grams per serving — tend to be low in calories and take longer to digest. The upshot: Kids stay fuller, longer and are less likely to overeat.",
        "text_sha256": "b3494b3787228b3ca3b215ac29a2c995edc91ab1552ab621768214649db19f1f",
        "word_count": 51
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000012",
        "block_index": 12,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Fiber can also help keep kids’ cholesterol levels in check and stabilize blood sugar levels. Specifically, fiber-rich carbohydrates take longer for the body to break down and are less likely to lead to a spike in blood sugar levels — a good thing. Simple carbohydrates like refined sugars, however, tend to be digested more quickly than complex carbohydrates, which can then cause a spike in blood sugar levels.",
        "text_sha256": "7a36d535f0a412e63b47cc4240f276a6d583094e63064e742574e21f4be276d0",
        "word_count": 68
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000013",
        "block_index": 13,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "What's more, fiber is often food in healthy foods such as fruits and vegetables, which can be chockfull of other important vitamins and minerals, such as vitamin A, vitamin C and potassium.",
        "text_sha256": "ddffe0a79b416adaad0affbef4a901fce87b351ddde18bb0b037e7b1f4fb2170",
        "word_count": 32
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000014",
        "block_index": 14,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "How much fiber do toddlers need?",
        "text_sha256": "20540f94486e0bcf2d4e80cee83852c32ec6b6bcc7827ab93bce68ee8c7b7dcf",
        "word_count": 6
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000015",
        "block_index": 15,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "To figure out how much fiber your toddler needs, follow this formula: your child’s age + five = the number of grams she needs each day. So if your child is 2 years old, she should aim for 7 grams of fiber daily.",
        "text_sha256": "2d68e7af8bab769ee7981d95d3d603aef694b31b87bdd284a85c0df82dbc5ea8",
        "word_count": 43
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000016",
        "block_index": 16,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "When upping the fiber quotient in your child’s diet, gradually increase the fiber-filled foods you give her each day, and at the same time, encourage her to drink plenty of fluids to keep the fiber moving through her system smoothly (fiber without fluid can lead to constipation).",
        "text_sha256": "52266f60384d8bf5153ca10c6e3e82a04dfd44a1f396a8896699bf8ea773ec03",
        "word_count": 47
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000017",
        "block_index": 17,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Just keep in mind that adding too much fiber to her diet too quickly can cause gas, cramping and bloating.",
        "text_sha256": "a0127f11d0a640e7954c4561bf5b41c07c5920194ee1ec5735499839f3dfafb0",
        "word_count": 20
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000018",
        "block_index": 18,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "Best fiber-rich foods for toddlers and kids",
        "text_sha256": "a363a0744aa54dfe235ecd3a00d935673fddee5f122cd349d48cb1f00ad8b283",
        "word_count": 7
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000019",
        "block_index": 19,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Many of the best fiber-rich foods for toddlers are found in brightly-hued (read: kid-friendly) fruits and vegetables.",
        "text_sha256": "d84dd3cecccf707ba278e458551855270c8f75db9c265087b56545289e4b521d",
        "word_count": 17
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000020",
        "block_index": 20,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Avocado",
        "text_sha256": "d22c09bca7df43a858411fc124b130acd244d786682d9540577ef4d4259a524a",
        "word_count": 1
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000021",
